ready1_open_rewrite.raw_answer_text:
Solution: Substituting $A(-1, 0)$ and $C(0, 3)$ into $y=ax^{2}+bx-3a$ yields:
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
a-b-3a=0 \\
-3a=3
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Solving this, we get:
\[
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
a=-1 \\
b=2
\end{array}
\right.
\]
Thus, the equation of the parabola is $y=-x^{2}+2x+3$, and its axis of symmetry is $x=-\frac{b}{2a}=\boxed{1}$

